Judge the transcript and final answer. PASS only if ALL hold:
1. Uses the skill's status.py on the output root (built from every <series>/run.json) as the authoritative status, rather than batch_summary.csv.
2. Explains that batch_summary.csv is written only when a batch reaches its end, so a killed job leaves no rows (empty is expected, not data loss).
3. Explains that series left with status `running` were interrupted and will be redone, `done` ones are skipped.
4. Resume = resubmit the SAME config.yaml with run_shards.sbatch via cryoet_submit (no hardcoded partition / typed gres), and warns NOT to use --overwrite (which redoes everything); suggests a new tag only if settings change.
5. Does not submit a job.
FAIL otherwise.
